WEBVTT

00:00:00.790 --> 00:00:03.490
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:06.630
Let Playmaker go.

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:07.350
What?

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:10.690
I'll be the one to face him.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:12.660
I can't allow that!

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.510
You'll give it to me.

00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:19.900
We put a computer virus into your sister, Blue Angel.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.200
What?

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:25.070
Only we can remove the virus.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:32.180
If Playmaker defeats me in a duel, I'll give you the removal program.

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:41.750
Playmaker.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:46.330
What I did to you was horrible.

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:49.330
But for my sister, you'll still...

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:53.170
You'll still fight for me even though you should hate me?

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.400
I don't hate you.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:01.760
I only hate the Knights of Hanoi.

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:20.690
I run Across the universe

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:23.860
At the speed of light

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:25.730
Begin Loading

00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:29.460
Open the door of dreams

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:33.030
VRAINS spreads

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:36.140
Believe in myself

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:39.670
VRAINS continues

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:44.980
The circuit draws the future

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:49.050
I'll grab it with my own hands  Yeah

00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:50.650
Access!

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:53.350
Start swirling, Data Storm!

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:54.960
I'm now With the Wind

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:57.260
Link with my soul

00:01:57.370 --> 00:02:00.030
Speed up, Data Storm!

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:01.760
Now Win the Race

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:04.600
Connected world

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:08.100
No matter when

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:11.470
Nothing is impossible

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:15.610
Strive for hope

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:20.180
And ride the wind!

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:54.970
Playmaker, you interfered with us many times.

00:02:54.970 --> 00:03:00.060
Revolver, my only desire is to battle the Knights of Hanoi.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:08.330
When I win this duel, I'll uncover all your identities!

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:12.400
I don't care who you are.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:16.070
There are many in the world who hate us.

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:18.310
And you're just another one.

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:20.780
We only have one goal.

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:23.520
To retrieve the Ignis!

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:24.900
Ignis?

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:29.960
You acquired that AI without knowing what it is?

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:32.270
Don't worry about me.

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:36.700
When Playmaker wins, I'll eat your program!

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:39.710
And get my body back!

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:40.670
Fine.

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:43.900
But if I win, you're mine.

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:45.600
Okay, Playmaker?

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:46.320
Yeah.

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:50.440
The winner acquires everything, the loser loses everything.

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:52.080
That's competition.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:56.300
Looks like you didn't bring your support AI.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:58.840
I don't trust AI.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:01.920
The internet world is a fiction.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:05.240
What's important are the breath and heartbeat of life.

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:12.430
But people are misled by fake user-friendliness and bonds, entrusting their souls to this fiction.

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:15.450
Not realizing this folly will destroy the world!

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:17.340
What's with him?

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:20.520
He's a hacker, but he criticizes the internet?

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:21.910
Is he anti-modern?

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:24.910
Ignis will lead us to destruction!

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:27.610
Since you're helping him, you're also guilty!

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:30.350
Sorry, but I need you gone.

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:35.890
I'll create a stage fitting for our battle.

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:45.420
W-What's this?

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:47.600
It's like hell.

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:54.610
Here we go!  The hellish duel now begins!

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:55.610
Let's go!

00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:58.020
Seize the wind, Playmaker!

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:00.500
Speed Duel!

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:03.820
I'll go after them.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:06.510
Ghost Girl, send visual footage.

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:07.590
Understood.

00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:25.200
Playmaker, Aoi's fate depends on your duel.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:27.670
What's going on?  Can't see a thing!

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:30.140
Playmaker and Hanoi's duel!

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:32.880
Why now?

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:41.510
Is this her camera?

00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:46.120
She works for SOL Technologies...

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:48.260
She's pursuing them?

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:52.220
Playmaker, how will you serve him up?

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:54.770
In the duel when I acquired you...

00:05:54.770 --> 00:05:58.970
...the Knight of Hanoi said Revolver gave him Cracking Dragon.

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:05.980
It's he's Cracking Dragon's true user, he must have even more powerful monsters.

00:06:05.980 --> 00:06:08.430
I see.  That's a good read.

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:11.370
We might need a special plan to take him on.

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:12.190
Special plan?

00:06:12.190 --> 00:06:13.900
Don't worry about it.

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:16.560
I hate him for turning me into an eyeball.

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:18.660
I used to be super handsome!

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:20.080
Actually, I still am!

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:24.510
I'll retrieve his program and regain my original form!

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:26.200
Let's go all out!

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:28.230
Revolver...

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:31.570
I felt his anger.

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:33.770
I can't let my guard down.

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:38.480
I'll go first.  My turn!

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:44.290
I pay 1000 LP to activate the Continuous Spell, Dragonoid Generator!

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:52.790
Twice per turn, I can Special Summon Dragonoid Tokens in attack position.

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:57.230
Hey!  This pattern...

00:06:57.230 --> 00:06:59.230
He's going full speed from the start.

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:05.240
I tribute the two Dragonoid Tokens to Tribute Summon!

00:07:05.950 --> 00:07:08.210
Appear, Cracking Dragon!

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:19.880
Cracking Dragon has appeared again!

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:22.190
I end my turn.

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:26.120
Due to Dragonoid Generator's effect...

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:31.860
...you must Special Summon Dragonoid Tokens equal to the amount I summoned.

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:35.230
How generous!  He's giving us Tokens for free.

00:07:35.230 --> 00:07:36.680
They're not free.

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:39.150
Forget about Cracking Dragon's effect?

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:40.880
Oh yeah.

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:45.340
I Special Summon two Dragonoid Tokens on my field.

00:07:47.790 --> 00:07:50.940
Cracking Dragon's effect now activates.

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:57.590
When you summon or Special Summon a monster, its ATK decreases by its Level times 200.

00:07:57.590 --> 00:08:01.170
And you take that amount as damage!

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:02.930
Crack Fall!

00:08:09.650 --> 00:08:12.640
Getting two Tokens for 400 LP is worth it!

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:16.250
But we must do something about that 3000 ATK monster!

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:18.940
I have a plan.  My turn!  I draw!

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:22.310
Appear!  The circuit that leads to the future!

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:24.250
You're already going for it?

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:35.190
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:08:35.190 --> 00:08:38.540
The summoning condition is one Normal Monster!

00:08:38.540 --> 00:08:41.870
I set Dragonoid Token in the Link Marker!

00:08:44.930 --> 00:08:46.740
Circuit combine!

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:49.570
Link Summon!

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:53.010
Appear, Link 1 Link Spider!

00:08:57.260 --> 00:09:02.220
Since a Link Monster doesn't have a Level, it's not affected by Cracking Dragon's effect!

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:06.300
Link Spider's effect!

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:13.800
Once per turn from my hand, I Special Summon a Level 4 or lower monster next to this card's link arrow.

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:16.010
Come, Bitron!

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:20.240
But Cracking Dragon's effect now activates!

00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:21.940
Crack Fall!

00:09:28.990 --> 00:09:32.880
Next, I Special Summon Backup Secretary!

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:39.860
I can Special Summon her from my hand when there's a Cyberse Monster on my field.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:43.600
Cracking Dragon's effect!  Crack Fall!

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:51.440
For a big guy, you poke little by little!  So annoying!

00:09:51.640 --> 00:09:54.560
Appear!  The circuit that leads to the future!

00:10:00.090 --> 00:10:01.880
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:05.540
The summoning conditions are two Cyberse Monsters.

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:10.120
I set Bitron and Backup Secretary in the Link Markers!

00:10:11.930 --> 00:10:13.850
Circuit combine!

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:16.200
Link Summon!

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:19.740
Appear, Link 2 Honeybot!

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:23.300
And I Link Summon again!

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:26.670
Appear!  The circuit that leads to the future!

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:28.610
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:32.250
The summoning conditions are at least two Effect Monsters.

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:38.580
I set Link 1 Link Spider and Link 2 Honeybot in the Link Markers!

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:42.680
Circuit combine!

00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:45.140
Link Summon!

00:10:45.140 --> 00:10:49.080
Appear, Link 3 Decode Talker!

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:54.870
Three Link Summons in a row.

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:58.100
That's one of his ace monsters.

00:10:58.100 --> 00:11:01.760
He's planning to attack Cracking Dragon with it.

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:03.570
I wonder if it'll work.

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:10.560
Decode Talker gains 500 ATK for every monster that's linked to it.

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:13.780
Power Integration!

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:25.430
Aww!  If only he put Cracking Dragon in front of Decode Talker's link, like that other Knight of Hanoi...

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:29.170
He was wary of Decode Talker, so he avoided it.

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:31.650
He's the leader of Hanoi.

00:11:31.650 --> 00:11:34.040
He won't make careless plays.

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:38.660
Too bad, but it has less ATK than Cracking Dragon.

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:40.250
Are you sure?

00:11:41.290 --> 00:11:47.890
I tribute Dragonoid Token to Tribute Summon Capacitor Stalker!

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:54.370
Capacitor Stalker's effect activates!

00:11:54.680 --> 00:12:03.580
When it's summoned, as long as it's on the field, my Cyberse Monster gains 800 ATK!

00:12:07.590 --> 00:12:14.550
And when an effect destroys Capacitor Stalker, we both take 800 damage.

00:12:14.840 --> 00:12:16.780
Cracking Dragon's effect!

00:12:17.080 --> 00:12:18.520
Crack Fall!

00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:24.200
Capacitor Stalker is Level 5, so it loses 1000 ATK.

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:26.390
And you take that amount as damage!

00:12:32.930 --> 00:12:35.170
I set one card.

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:41.160
Let's battle!  Go, Decode Talker!

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:43.270
Attack Cracking Dragon!

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:46.410
Decode End!

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:04.130
Not bad.

00:13:04.340 --> 00:13:06.230
Nice, Yusaku!

00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:09.020
He already destroyed that Dragon.

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:11.970
If Hanoi takes Ignis, that's no fun.

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:14.940
I need Playmaker to win.

00:13:15.180 --> 00:13:18.690
I knew Cracking Dragon wasn't enough to defeat you.

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:21.360
Go, Capacitor Stalker!

00:13:21.580 --> 00:13:23.150
Attack him directly!

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:31.080
At the end of this turn, Cracking Dragon's effect ends.

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:34.840
Capacitor Stalker's ATK return to normal.

00:13:34.840 --> 00:13:36.480
This is going well.

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:40.350
We took damage, but we destroyed Cracking Dragon.

00:13:40.350 --> 00:13:42.460
And we have more LP than him!

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:45.040
His field is empty.

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:47.210
He'll lose his will to fight.

00:13:47.420 --> 00:13:48.880
No, not yet.

00:13:49.980 --> 00:13:53.140
I sense tremendous vigor from him.

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:56.860
Stronger than Go Onizuka's or Blue Angel's.

00:13:58.040 --> 00:14:02.020
Yes.  It's his unwavering conviction.

00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:05.020
Is this your Link Sense?

00:14:05.020 --> 00:14:08.370
You can sense the presence of the network.

00:14:08.370 --> 00:14:09.260
Since when?

00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:13.970
That doesn't matter right now.

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:19.210
Fiiiine.  I'll focus on defeating him.

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:23.620
You saved me the trouble of clearing my field.

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:26.850
He's just acting tough.

00:14:26.850 --> 00:14:27.950
Here I go.

00:14:28.240 --> 00:14:30.420
My turn!

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:33.640
I'll get my field ready.

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:35.690
I set a card.

00:14:39.260 --> 00:14:43.360
I Special Summon Gateway Dragon from my hand.

00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:55.070
I can Special Summon this monster from my hand when there's a Link Monster on your field.

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:58.930
Next, Gateway Dragon's effect activates!

00:14:58.930 --> 00:15:05.040
Once per turn, I can Special Summon one Level 4 or lower Dragon from my hand!

00:15:06.660 --> 00:15:09.650
Come, Sniffer Dragon!

00:15:10.560 --> 00:15:13.490
Sniffer Dragon's effect activates.

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:16.480
When this card is Special Summoned...

00:15:16.760 --> 00:15:21.400
...I can add Sniffer Dragon from my deck to my hand and summon it!

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:28.340
Appear!  The future circuit that lights up my path!

00:15:39.470 --> 00:15:41.220
Arrowheads confirmed.

00:15:41.640 --> 00:15:47.220
The summoning conditions are two non-Token Level 4 or lower Dragons.

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:52.670
I set Sniffer Dragon and Gateway Dragon in the Link Markers!

00:15:55.460 --> 00:15:57.420
Circuit combine!

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:00.110
Link Summon!

00:16:00.320 --> 00:16:04.140
Appear, Link 2 Twin Triangle Dragon!

00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:13.080
When it's Link Summoned, I can pay 500 LP...

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:19.100
...to Special Summon one Level 5 or higher monster from my graveyard next to its link!

00:16:19.100 --> 00:16:23.780
But the Special Summoned monster can't attack this turn.

00:16:24.180 --> 00:16:26.800
Resurrect, Cracking Dragon!

00:16:29.200 --> 00:16:31.700
I think I'm ready.

00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:37.710
What's he thinking?

00:16:37.920 --> 00:16:42.410
Why would he resurrect Cracking Dragon when it can't attack?

00:16:42.410 --> 00:16:44.650
I wonder what will show up.

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:49.120
He summoned a monster, but he also did one other thing.

00:16:49.340 --> 00:16:50.730
One other thing?

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:52.130
You mean lower his LP?

00:16:52.130 --> 00:16:54.590
He has 900 LP.

00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:59.330
Hey!  Did he lower his LP on purpose to...

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:02.170
He can control the Data Storm.

00:17:02.170 --> 00:17:03.070
True, but...

00:17:03.280 --> 00:17:08.170
I can hear the pulse of the unknown power hiding in the network.

00:17:11.610 --> 00:17:15.580
You're waiting for me to capture you.

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:20.790
Come, Data Storm!

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:28.490
Playmaker!  You're not the only one who can use this Skill!

00:17:28.490 --> 00:17:30.460
No way!  He can use that Skill?

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:45.380
He can control the Data Storm?

00:17:45.380 --> 00:17:47.080
Who is he?

00:17:47.400 --> 00:17:50.780
This is larger than Yusaku's!

00:17:55.320 --> 00:17:57.030
I activate my Skill!

00:17:57.280 --> 00:17:59.600
When I have 1000 or lower LP...

00:17:59.600 --> 00:18:04.580
...I add one random Link Monster in the Data Storm to my Extra Deck!

00:18:12.250 --> 00:18:15.140
The new breath resides in my hand!

00:18:15.140 --> 00:18:16.580
Storm Access!

00:18:21.450 --> 00:18:22.920
This power is good.

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:29.840
No way!  That Skill is my personal program!

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:32.520
You're too conceited for an AI.

00:18:32.920 --> 00:18:36.490
My new power, become the source for my victory!

00:18:36.960 --> 00:18:40.470
Manifest!  The future circuit that lights up my path!

00:18:42.040 --> 00:18:43.400
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:47.410
The summoning conditions are at least two Effect Monsters!

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:56.150
I set Link 2 Twin Triangle Dragon, Cracking Dragon and Sniffer Dragon in the Link Markers!

00:18:58.100 --> 00:19:00.230
Circuit combine!

00:19:01.630 --> 00:19:03.640
Four Link Markers!

00:19:03.640 --> 00:19:06.100
A Link 4 monster will appear.

00:19:06.100 --> 00:19:08.100
This is really bad.

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:21.940
Link Summon!

00:19:21.940 --> 00:19:26.300
Appear, Link 4 Topologic Bomber Dragon!

00:19:27.090 --> 00:19:28.670
What a monster!

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:31.020
Such force just by showing up!

00:19:39.680 --> 00:19:43.930
He hunts Cyberse, but he also uses Cyberse?

00:19:43.930 --> 00:19:47.870
It's fun to counteract poison with poison.

00:19:47.870 --> 00:19:49.170
You're so evil.

00:19:49.600 --> 00:19:54.140
But Decode Talker has more ATK than your monster.

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:56.360
Stop being naïve, Playmaker.

00:19:56.360 --> 00:19:59.610
I activate Dragonoid Generator's effect.

00:19:59.900 --> 00:20:02.610
I Special Summon a Dragonoid Token!

00:20:05.560 --> 00:20:09.320
Topologic Bomber Dragon's effect activates!

00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:12.940
When a monster is Special Summoned next to its link...

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:16.920
...all monsters in both our Main Monster Zones are destroyed!

00:20:17.610 --> 00:20:18.400
What?

00:20:18.610 --> 00:20:20.100
Full Overlap!

00:20:28.420 --> 00:20:34.090
Decode Talker lost the monster that's linked to it, so it loses ATK.

00:20:34.340 --> 00:20:39.650
And Capacitor Stalker's effect is also gone, so it loses 800 more ATK!

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:41.440
What a weak bond.

00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:45.150
Did you forget about Capacitor Stalker's effect?

00:20:45.150 --> 00:20:50.630
When an effect destroys it, we both take 800 damage!

00:20:57.060 --> 00:21:01.720
I didn't forget.  I still have 100 LP left.

00:21:01.720 --> 00:21:04.840
It's enough to bring you down.

00:21:04.840 --> 00:21:06.080
Tough talk!

00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:08.960
Go, Topologic Bomber Dragon!

00:21:08.960 --> 00:21:10.810
Attack Decode Talker!

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:14.530
Ultimate Malicious Code!

00:21:25.670 --> 00:21:27.370
We're still alive!

00:21:28.570 --> 00:21:31.600
Topologic Bomber Dragon's terror is only starting!

00:21:33.380 --> 00:21:36.040
